# Language statistics
#
# GitHub sizes its language bar by bytes, and this repository carries 44 MB of
# notebooks and 69 MB of generated HTML against 350 KB of Python. Left alone it
# would be reported as an HTML project, which is the opposite of what it is.
#
# Nothing here hides content — every file stays browsable. These markers only
# keep generated and archival material out of the language statistics and out of
# diffs, so what shows is the code that was actually written.

# The superseded notebook version, kept as the record of what the rebuild
# replaced. It is history, not the current implementation.
Notebooks/**            linguist-documentation
Notebooks/**            linguist-generated=true

# That version's results, and this one's: rendered explanations and panels, not
# authored source.
outputs/**              linguist-vendored
Report/**               linguist-documentation

# Per-prediction records: data, not code.
artifacts/**            linguist-generated=true

# Notebooks produce enormous, unreadable diffs. Collapse them by default; the
# file is still viewable in full on GitHub.
*.ipynb                 linguist-documentation
*.ipynb                 -diff

# Treat the attribution records as text so they diff and blame sensibly, but
# never try to merge them — they are regenerated, not edited.
*.jsonl                 text -merge

# Normalise line endings so the repository behaves the same on any platform.
* text=auto
*.png                   binary
*.pdf                   binary
*.npy                   binary
*.safetensors           binary

# Archival material is stored exactly as it was produced. These files are a
# record of an earlier version of this work, so rewriting their line endings —
# even harmlessly — would make them no longer that record.
outputs/**              -text
Notebooks/**            -text
